    {
      "query": "queries.scm",
      "capabilities": [
        "calls",
        "references"
      ],
      "reason": "A call is stated under the name as written. `obj.method()` is a call to `method` with the receiver unknown, because JavaScript binds a property at run time; a call made through a variable that holds a function, through `fn.call`/`fn.apply`, through a computed member (`api[name]()`) or through `Reflect` is not stated at all."
    },
    {
      "query": "queries.scm",
      "capabilities": [
        "references"
      ],
      "reason": "A property that is read rather than called (`conn.timeout`) is not emitted. The grammar gives a read and a callee the same `member_expression`, JavaScript supplies no static type for the receiver, and a bare property name would resolve against every declaration of that name in the repository."
    },
    {
      "query": "queries.scm",
      "capabilities": [
        "definitions",
        "bindings",
        "scopes"
      ],
      "reason": "A name bound inside a function body -- by `const`, `let` or `var` below module level, by a destructuring pattern, by a `for` target, by `catch (e)` or by a parameter -- is not declared. Parameters are stated as the declaration's parameter shape, not as names of their own, and the names a destructuring pattern introduces are stated nowhere."
    },
    {
      "query": "queries.scm",
      "capabilities": [
        "definitions"
      ],
      "reason": "A module-level binding is declared only when it has an initialiser that holds a value: a literal, an object, an array, a call, a `new`, a member expression or another name. `let cache;` with no initialiser is not declared, and neither is a binding introduced by a top-level destructuring pattern."
    },
    {
      "query": "queries.scm",
      "capabilities": [
        "imports"
      ],
      "reason": "A module specifier is recorded exactly as written -- `./util`, `pkg/sub`, `node:fs`. Turning one into a file means running Node's resolution algorithm over `package.json` `exports`, `main` and `imports` maps and whatever aliases the bundler adds, which the project's own configuration decides. `import * as ns` binds a namespace whose members are not stated."
    },
    {
      "query": "queries.scm",
      "capabilities": [
        "modules",
        "definitions"
      ],
      "reason": "What a file exports can be computed at run time -- `Object.assign(module.exports, ...)`, a conditional `module.exports`, a getter on `exports`, a re-export behind a loop. Only the written forms are stated, and a re-export names the module it comes from, not the names it forwards."
    },
    {
      "query": "queries.scm",
      "capabilities": [
        "definitions"
      ],
      "reason": "JavaScript declares no types. A declaration's parameter shape is the source text of its parameter list, so nothing is stated about the type of any parameter, field, return value or module-level name; a JSDoc `@param` or `@returns` comment is not read."
    }
  ],
